					"6058a8a6": {
						"questionId": "6058a8a6",
						"textAnswers": {
							"answers": [
								{
									"value": "[80]Very little time for QRS Net this Tuesday, managed to get on air by 10:30 UTC. Checked propagation by having a look at FT8 segment lots of JA and USA stations so prospects looked fine. Unfortunately nothing in QRS CW segment! After few unanswered CQ calls I moved to 160, and on return spotted few signals on vk5arg SDR. vk2ki was just finishing with vk6nw, how convenient. Wayne was coming through very strong probably the best heard so far but the band noise was just as strong. By my S meter he (+ noise ) about S8.\nHe came back immediately and we started Reg Chew. Well into the chat my sone walked in to remand me to turn water to  hot water system we fixed earlier in the evening. Had to cut QSO with Wayne short to bleed hot water of air and just managed to sort out everything before tariff 2 power was turned  on by Alinta. Close shave. On return to radio band looked deserted , my signal was the only trace on vk5arg SDR. Persevered for a while and vk2wf came back for a brief exchange. On these occasion Adrian was using a hand key and going slowly which surprised me, last time I worked him on 160 m he was belting at some speed. After QRS net ended I moved to FT8 and DX were still coming through so I had a field day with UA,USA and JA contacts. One of the best DX nights this year. \n[160] Just one QSO with vk3acu. Jordan was copying me OK but I was struggling he was strong still just under my noise floor of S9. I captured our signals at vk5arg SDR and Jordan was considerably stronger than myself despite lower power. DXing on 160 m is really hard specially with a low  hanging  antenna. "
								}
							]
						}
					},
