						"textAnswers": {
							"answers": [
								{
									"value": "[20 m]\nDidn't make any attempt to work the EU cohort this week. \n\n\n[80 m]\nThe band sounded pretty good compared to 40 m.   Heard a number of VKs but didn't write down call signs.  One station I recognized was even slower than usual but time ran out waiting for a confirming call sign.    Other time was well spent transmitting 'Morse With Purpose' Cold War groups, according to the advertised timetable.  Could hear myself on Ironstone an acceptable 531. The VKs working towards a Cold War badge were using ZL SDRs to good effect, all copied the groups with 100 % accuracy.  Speed was only 15/10, at the lowest end of typical number stations' speed,  nonetheless, well done guys."
								}
							]
						}
					},
