			{
				"responseId": "ACYDBNh3CUM0wHuN8x-9QJBGw23HSoCVU_JT4lJ-oTLZD-PUdseahTKIHA68RljwPiZpvVs",
				"createTime": "2026-08-19T03:37:47.435Z",
				"lastSubmittedTime": "2026-08-19T03:37:47.435827Z",
				"answers": {
					"0e70c164": {
						"questionId": "0e70c164",
						"textAnswers": {
							"answers": [
								{
									"value": "I wasn't expecting much having watched the K-Index steadily climb to 4 over the course of the afternoon, yet when it was time don the headphones, flick the power switch and tune up, I was greeted by 40 m alive with activity.  And not just activity, but lovely strong signals.  A most unexpected joy.\n\nFirst up was an enjoyable three way QSO with James and Mark, VK3JFR and VK2KI.  Apart from the joy of a little round robin QSO, what really put a smile on my face was was how each was recognisable from their tone.  To start we were all a little off frequency, then together with James' and my fist and Mark's slight chirp, it was easy to identify the sender without callsigns.  Such fun.  Our final three-way 73 and shave-and-a-haircut exchange even gave David, VK3DBD, a chuckle, who chimed in with his HI.\n\nWith James and Mark off, David and I had a brief QSO despite him suffering QRM in the shack.  What started out as a very poor S3, jumped to a whopping S9+ when David switched to the correct antenna.  What a difference it made.\\n\\nI then tried my luck on 80 m, and was quickly answered by ZL2IR for a brief QSO.  That was followed by a really enjoyable rag-chew with George, VK2AOE.  It took a moment to recognise callsign from his antenna article in last week's RagChew.  We had a good chat about antennas, his Hermes SDR and walking in Tasmania.\n\nThen back to 40 m where I had a brief QSO with Rod, VK6KHZ.  Sadly the circuit didn't hold beyond signal reports.  Not to worry, as that was quickly followed by a chat with Carl, VK5CT, who I initially confused with Chris, VK1CT.\n\nAs though by magic, for my final QSO I moved back down to 80, and who should I hook up with, but Chris, VK1CT!  It's been a long time since we've had a good enough circuit to enjoy a long rag-chew, so made the most of it until it was time for me to QRT.\n\nAll in all it was a really enjoyable evening.  Thank-you."
								}
							]
						}
					},
