				"answers": {
					"0e70c164": {
						"questionId": "0e70c164",
						"textAnswers": {
							"answers": [
								{
									"value": "I thought, for a change I'd call CQ instead of listening to the Ironstone Range SDR. I called on and around 7025 kHz for quite some time but didn't get any takers. I heard VK2KI at S9 in contact with VK2WP on 7033 kHz, or there abouts. I called both Mark and Wal after the conclusion of their contact but didn't receive a reply. Just as well I suppose because my noise floor had risen to S7 which would have made copy very difficult.\n\nI listened to the Ironstone Range for another half an hour or so where I heard VK5AO. The QRN and multiple stations on the same frequency was quite distracting so I gave it away.\n\n"
								}
							]
						}
					},
