									"value": "I have missed the past three weeks of the net as Anne and I went over East to catch up with my sister and her partner and brought back my old 1949 Land Rover from Broken Hill where it has been sitting in a shed for over 30 years.\nThose who have not used one of these early Landys in the bush have missed out of one of life's great experiences. I know you Tojo drivers will be shaking your heads. \nThose early Rovers are so easy to manoeuvre, they skip over sand without dropping tyre pressure and if you rolled one you should lose your licence for life. \nTo give an idea of how stable they were, let me tell you about an experience I had when wrecking one 50 years ago. We had put a rope over the vehicle and winched it onto its side so we could attack the task from its underside. As we let the tension off on the winch the vehicle promptly went back on its feet. Try that test on a Tojo and you will have difficulty getting it back on its feet.\nSomuch for my excuse for being absent for the past few weeks.\n\nNow this week I put out a few CQ's while working on some gear but did not hear a nibble. However I did spend a couple of hours following multiple conversations on 40 and 80 metres. It was particularly nice to hear the patience of operators working the slower stations.\n\nI will be away again for the next two weeks visiting the harmonics in Perth. I will also get to the NCRG hamfest and am going to swing down the coast to stir up VK6FN. I suspect the missing essential component of his care will thus be provided.\n\n\n"
								}
							]
						}
					},
