			{
				"responseId": "ACYDBNhZJu29zf3exKFWiPNmwIymbUFno7cEp8QYUs2duZ8Z0jjcSGA-1xWpU2BkqaCkJLU",
				"createTime": "2026-08-20T01:06:48.319Z",
				"lastSubmittedTime": "2026-08-20T01:06:48.319901Z",
				"answers": {
					"0e70c164": {
						"questionId": "0e70c164",
						"textAnswers": {
							"answers": [
								{
									"value": "40m was remarkably quiet, band-noise-wise for me this week.  So quiet in fact that I was able to not use my phasing-type noise canceller at all - that's a first!  Could it be the installation of a new router here that's made the difference I wonder?\n\nIt was nice to catch up again with Wal VK2WP up at Bathurst.  You never know with Wal what interesting bit of kit he might be using, and this week it was a vintage Drake 2NT 60 Watt transmitter;  sounded good.  I noticed that Phil VK4BVM was listening in via the Ironstone Range KiwiSDR.\n\nTuning around after finishing with Wal, I heard our editor Lance VK7TO who was a really solid RSN 592;  I thought that Lance was calling CQ, so I popped in my callsign.  Turned out that I was wrong;  Lance was in QSO with James VK3JFR (also RSN 592 here) so he sent me a QRX while he sorted out the reports with James.  He then brought me in and we started a three-way QSO, which went very well.  Great fun and challenging on CW - should be more of it!"
								}
							]
						}
					},
					"7c22f4a2": {
