					"6058a8a6": {
						"questionId": "6058a8a6",
						"textAnswers": {
							"answers": [
								{
									"value": "[20m]\nWonders never cease!  This week I was actually on-time and heard Manny VK3DRQ (albeit very weak here) chatting to Mike DL3YZ, before I caught up with Mike myself.  Mike was RSN 421 from his ham clubroom Yagi, and he reported 231 - so a bit of s struggle for Mike.  Great to know that the macheteing to access the clubroom was worthwhile.\n\nRoss M0NNK/P was RSN 231 into the Ironstone Range KiwiSDR, and like recent weeks, not a sausage was heard here.\n\nI did hear Patrick VK2IOW talking to Mike then Ross, and then to round it all out, Mike chatting to Ross.\n\n[80m]\nAfter dinner I re-adjusted my antenna coupler to 80m, and found the band noise to be remarkably low about S3) as well - so I decided to not use my noise canceller on that band as well.  I had a nice rag chew with Greg VK5KFG at Willunga;  conditions were great and Greg had a nice RSN 593.  And the good conditions continued West and I hooked up wth Wayne VK6NW who was pounding in with a remarkable RSB 583.  Aren't we lucky to have such good propagation;  I love 80m!  \n\nUnfortunately I needed to have an early night so had to give the good conditions a miss and head off the bed."
								}
							]
						}
					},
